---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { getPieces, PLATFORM_META, TYPE_META } from '../lib/pieces';
const pieces = await getPieces();
---
<Base title="About" description="What the Design Lounge is, why it exists, and the rules every piece follows.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="About" title="A lounge, <i>not a feed</i>" blurb="Design galleries are mostly screenshots of other people’s work, scrolling past. This is the opposite: a small number of pieces you can sit with, run, read, and take home." />
  <div class="wrap about">
    <section class="block">
      <h2 class="display h3">What it is</h2>
      <p>Design Lounge is a catalogue of interface pieces: whole screens, single components, animations, layouts, product patterns and entire design languages, for the web, mobile web, native-feel mobile apps, PWAs and tablets. Every piece is live, not a picture. Every piece is one self-contained HTML file you can read in a minute. And every piece ships with a brief: a markdown document written for a coding agent, precise enough that the agent can rebuild the piece in your stack without ever seeing the demo.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="block">
      <h2 class="display h3">Why briefs, not screenshots</h2>
      <p>“Make it look like this” with a screenshot gets you a guess. A brief with a token block, a motion table and an acceptance checklist gets you the thing. Agents are good at numbers and lists; they are bad at taste. So the taste is done here, once, and written down in the form agents consume best. You keep the judgement, they keep the typing.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="block">
      <h2 class="display h3">House rules</h2>
      <ul class="rules">
        <li><b>One idea per piece.</b> A sidebar piece is a great sidebar, not a sidebar plus a dashboard.</li>
        <li><b>Real copy, no placeholders.</b> No lorem ipsum, no “Heading 1”, no emoji.</li>
        <li><b>Motion has a reason.</b> Feedback, hierarchy, continuity, or one moment of delight. Reduced motion always respected.</li>
        <li><b>No dependencies.</b> A piece is one file: inline CSS, inline JS, inline SVG. Google Fonts are the only outside resource.</li>
        <li><b>Accessible by default.</b> Semantic elements, visible focus, ≥ 4.5:1 body contrast, ≥ 40px targets on phones.</li>
        <li><b>Numbers, not adjectives.</b> Briefs say 320ms and <code>cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)</code>, never “smooth”.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="block stats">
      <h2 class="display h3">The floor today</h2>
      <div class="stat-grid">
        {Object.entries(TYPE_META).map(([k, v]) => <a href={`/rooms/${k}`} class="stat"><span class="display n">{String(pieces.filter((p) => p.data.type === k).length).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span class="mono">{v.label}</span></a>)}
        {Object.entries(PLATFORM_META).map(([k, v]) => <a href={`/platforms/${k}`} class="stat"><span class="display n">{String(pieces.filter((p) => p.data.platform === k).length).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span class="mono">{v.label}</span></a>)}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="block">
      <h2 class="display h3">Use</h2>
      <p>Take the briefs and the source. Build products with them. Change the tokens to match your brand. Attribution is appreciated, not required. The one thing not to do is republish the catalogue as a catalogue.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="block">
      <h2 class="display h3">Colophon</h2>
      <p>Type is Fraunces (display), Instrument Sans (text) and JetBrains Mono (labels and numbers). The site is static HTML built with Astro, with a few hundred lines of vanilla JavaScript for the search, filters and device frames. Demos run in sandboxed iframes at native size and are scaled with a transform, so what you see in a card is the real thing, not a thumbnail.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { display: flex; flex-direction: column; margin-top: 40px; }
  .block { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 260px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 32px; padding: 36px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .block:first-child { border-top-color: var(--ink); }
  .block p { max-width: 66ch; font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-2); text-wrap: pretty; }
  .block p + p { margin-top: 14px; }
  .rules { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; font-size: 15.5px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 66ch; }
  .rules b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .rules code { background: var(--paper-2); border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: .05em .35em; border-radius: 4px; }
  .stat-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(140px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  .stat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; padding: 16px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-lg); transition: border-color var(--t-fast); }
  .stat:hover { border-color: var(--ink); }
  .stat .n { font-size: 40px; line-height: 1; }
  .stat .mono { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .block { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 12px; } }
</style>
